CONTEXT Reverse

PURPOSE PATTERN Specification
{+ This specification defines the reverse of a list. +}
PATTERN Specification
    CLASSIFY Empty, NonEmpty ISA List
    RELATION head[NonEmpty*Element] [UNI,TOT]
    RELATION tail[NonEmpty*List]    [UNI,TOT]
    RELATION last[NonEmpty*Element] [UNI,TOT]
    RELATION init[NonEmpty*List]    [UNI,TOT]

    RULE r0 : V[Empty] |- I[Empty]
    RULE r1 : init;I[Empty] = tail;I[Empty]
    RULE r2 : init;head |- head
    RULE r3 : tail;last |- last
    RULE r4 : head;head~ /\ tail;tail~ |- I[NonEmpty]
    RULE r5 : head~;(I/\tail;I[Empty];tail~);last |- I[Element]
    RULE r6 : init;tail = tail;init
ENDPATTERN

PURPOSE PATTERN Implementation
{+ This pattern defines the ConsLeft representation of a list. +}
PATTERN Implementation
    CLASSIFY EmptyLeft, ConsLeft ISA ListLeft
    CLASSIFY EmptyRight, ConsRight ISA ListRight

    RELATION sem[ListLeft*List] [UNI,TOT]
    PURPOSE RELATION sem[ListLeft*List]
    {+ This relation provides the semantics in the ConsLeft representation of a list. +}
    RELATION sem[ListRight*List] [UNI,TOT]
    PURPOSE RELATION sem[ListRight*List]
    {+ This relation provides the semantics in the ConsLeft representation of a list. +}

    RELATION reverse[ListLeft*ListRight] [UNI,TOT]
    PURPOSE RELATION reverse[ListLeft*ListRight]
    {+ This relation provides the semantics of the reverse of a list. +}

    RULE SemReverse : sem~;reverse;sem |- I
    RULE SemEmpty : I[EmptyLeft];sem[ListLeft*List];sem[ListRight*List]~;I[EmptyRight]
ENDPATTERN

ENDCONTEXT